{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794457780,"nonce":"gZrh1wcATmqv0Q3iOHdCAh0CiAY=","title":"Explore: list texts by a 'best' order, not by key","message":"GET /api/documents pages by entry key, (user_id, document_id) (f0f6df0), so every filter has an index in that order: public entries by user_document_public_idx (migration 0009), each tag value by user_document_tag_value_idx, merged with UNION ALL. That suits an API listing every text, but Explore shows them grouped by importer in hash order.\n\nGive the UI its own listing in a 'best' order: decide what the score is, and recompute it in a batch (say daily), so a cursor's order holds still between runs. A tag filter in that order needs the score on user_document_tag with an index (kind, value, score DESC, user_id, document_id) WHERE public, kept in step by triggers; and the unfiltered list needs one on user_document. Newest first has the same shape, imported_at in the score's place.\n\nuser_document_public_imported_idx and user_document_user_imported_idx (0007) aren't used by the list any more: drop them, or use them for this.","files":null}]}